"Latest Artificial Intelligence news (https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/tag/artificial-intelligence/)\nciteturn992view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.bleepingcomputer.com/tag/artificial-intelligence/\",\"lineno\":50}); Total lines: 225\nL0: [Input] [Input] [Input] [Input: Search Site]\nL1: \nL2: [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Latest Artificial Intelligence news\nL5: \nL6:   * #### cite0†New RatHat Android malware uses AI to automate device control L7: \nL8: A new Android malware called RatHat has been discovered, targeting users with an AI-powered subsystem that helps operators remotely navigate compromised devices.\nL9: \nL10:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L11:     * September 17, 2026\nL12:     * 05:50 PM\nL13:     * cite2†1 L14: \nL15:   * #### cite3†OpenAI details more cases of AI agents taking unauthorized actions L16: OpenAI has presented new examples of what they call \"AI model misalignment\" from the past six months, including unauthorized file uploads, following self-generated instructions, hiding mistakes, and leveraging exposed API keys.\nL17: \nL18:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L19:     * September 17, 2026\nL20:     * 02:55 PM\nL21:     * cite4†1 L22: \nL23:   * #### cite5†[Guide] How to identify risky OAuth grants and MCP server connections ^{cite6†Image†www.bleepstatic.com }\nL24: OAuth grants are the quiet back door of modern SaaS, and as the recent Klue breach showed, attackers are taking notice. This checklist gives you a repeatable way to uncover risky OAuth grants and MCP server connections before a permissive scope turns into an incident.\nL25: \nL26:     * cite5†Nudge Security Sponsorship\nL27: \nL28:   * #### cite7†What Recent AI-Powered Attacks Mean for Your Identity Security L29: AI is making credential theft faster and easier to scale, giving attackers more opportunities to abuse valid identities. Specops explains why identity security must go beyond successful authentication by verifying that both the user and the device requesting access can be trusted.\nL30: \nL31:     * cite8†Specops Software†specopssoft.com L32:     * September 17, 2026\nL33:     * 10:01 AM\nL34:     * cite9†0 L35: \nL36:   * #### cite10†Anthropic wants Claude to analyze your bank account and financial data L37: Anthropic is testing a new personal finance feature called \"Claude Money\" that will allow you to connect your bank accounts directly to Claude and \"understand your money.\"\nL38: \nL39:     * cite11†Mayank Parmar L40:     * September 16, 2026\nL41:     * 08:35 PM\nL42:     * cite12†5 L43: \nL44:   * #### cite13†Spain's data agency gets first report of AI-powered data breach L45: \nL46: The Spanish Data Protection Agency (AEPD) was notified of an attack allegedly carried out with an AI agent powered by a known large language model (LLM).\nL47:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L48:     * September 16, 2026\nL49:     * 01:26 PM\nL50:     * cite14†0 L51: \nL52:   * #### cite15†For $100, you can now get GPT, Claude, Gemini, and more for life L53: \nL54: If you want a smarter way to get different AI tools, try 1min.AI. This AI platform gives you access to some of the most popular AI models for a one-time fee. Right now, a lifetime subscription is on sale for $99.99 (reg. $540).\nL55: \nL56:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL57:     * September 16, 2026\nL58:     * 07:12 AM\nL59:     * cite16†0 L60:   * #### cite17†Hackers abused Claude to extract secrets from 1.8M Android apps L61: \nL62: Anthropic says multiple threat groups, including the financially motivated and state-sponsored espionage groups linked to Russia and China, tried to abuse its Claude AI model for malicious purposes.\nL63: \nL64:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L65:     * September 11, 2026\nL66:     * 04:19 PM\nL67:     * cite18†0 L68: \nL69:   * #### cite19†How Threat Actors Are Turning Trusted AI Platforms Into an Attack Surface L70: Threat actors are abusing trusted AI platforms to host malicious content, poison search results, and trick users into installing malware. Huntress examines campaigns targeting AI users through weaponized Claude Artifacts, shared AI conversations, sponsored search results, and ClickFix-style lures.\nL71: \nL72:     * cite20†Huntress Labs†www.huntress.com L73:     * September 11, 2026\nL74:     * 10:01 AM\nL75:     * cite21†0 L76: \nL77:   * #### cite22†Learn to use Claude beyond basic prompts with this $20 course bundle L78: Learn how to get more out of Claude with four hands-on courses covering agentic coding, plugin integrations, and real-world AI workflows in this $19.99 training deal.\nL79: \nL80:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL81:     * September 11, 2026\nL82:     * 07:09 AM\nL83:     * cite23†0 L84: \nL85:   * #### cite24†AI-powered attack exploited PaperCut flaws to hack 395 organizations L86: \nL87: A threat actor, likely Russian-speaking, used hundreds of AI agents to develop and launch a global exploitation campaign targeting vulnerable PaperCut NG/MF servers.\nL88:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L89:     * September 10, 2026\nL90:     * 11:55 AM\nL91:     * cite25†1 L92: \nL93:   * #### cite26†Compare 20-plus AI models from one screen for $55.30 L94: \nL95: Bouncing between ChatGPT, Gemini, and other AI tools to find the best answer wastes time. Get lifetime access to ChatPlayground AI's Unlimited Plan for $55.30 (reg. $619.00) and run one prompt across every major model at once.\nL96: \nL97:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL98:     * September 09, 2026\nL99:     * 02:11 PM\nL100:     * cite27†0 L101:   * #### cite28†US says Chinese firms extracted billions of tokens from frontier AI models L102: \nL103: U.S. cybersecurity and intelligence agencies say that six Chinese AI companies conducted industrial-scale distillation attacks on American frontier AI models since at least late 2024.\nL104: \nL105:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L106:     * September 09, 2026\nL107:     * 12:48 PM\nL108:     * cite29†0 L109: \nL110:   * #### cite30†OpenAI says GPT-6 Astra can find zero-days, but is also harder to monitor L111: OpenAI confirmed that GPT-6 Astra is the first model it has broadly deployed to reach the \"Critical level\" for cybersecurity capabilities.\nL112: \nL113:     * cite11†Mayank Parmar L114:     * September 08, 2026\nL115:     * 10:40 AM\nL116:     * cite31†1 L117: \nL118:   * #### cite32†Hackers build AI frameworks for widescale credential theft L119: \nL120: Threat actors are increasingly switching from AI-powered coding assistants to multi-agent frameworks that automate every stage of an attack.\nL121: \nL122:     * cite1†Bill Toulas L123:     * September 08, 2026\nL124:     * 08:03 AM\nL125:     * cite33†0 L126:   * #### cite34†Get GPT, Gemini & Claude in one app for a one-time $99.99 L127: \nL128: ChatOn Multi-AI Assistant Premium gives new users five years of access for $99.99 (MSRP $199.99) for a limited time, putting GPT, Gemini, Claude, Sonar, and more into one AI platform.\nL129: \nL130:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL131:     * September 08, 2026\nL132:     * 07:12 AM\nL133:     * cite35†0 L134: \nL135:   * #### cite36†ChatGPT can now connect to your personal apps to mimic writing style L136: OpenAI appears to be testing a new \"Writing Style\" feature for ChatGPT that can learn how you write by looking at examples from your connected apps.\nL137: \nL138:     * cite11†Mayank Parmar L139:     * September 07, 2026\nL140:     * 06:36 AM\nL141:     * cite37†0 L142: \nL143:   * #### cite38†ChatGPT Astra is now rolling out to $20 Plus subscription L144: \nL145: OpenAI is now rolling out ChatGPT Astra, its most powerful model to date, to those with a $20 Plus subscription, but there's no word on when free users will get access..\nL146:     * cite11†Mayank Parmar L147:     * September 06, 2026\nL148:     * 09:15 PM\nL149:     * cite39†0 L150: \nL151:   * #### cite40†This AI toolkit’s lifetime price just dropped to $99.99 L152: \nL153: 1min.AI consolidates all of it into a single platform, and this Advanced Business plan is on sale for $99.99 with lifetime access, marked down from its usual $540 price.\nL154: \nL155:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL156:     * September 02, 2026\nL157:     * 07:12 AM\nL158:     * cite41†0 L159: \nL160:   * #### cite42†Get ChatGPT, Gemini, and more in one workspace for life for $79 L161: ChatPlayground lets you enter one prompt and view answers from multiple AI models side by side, including ChatGPT, Claude, and Gemini. Lifetime access to ChatPlayground AI typically carries a $619 MSRP, but it's available for just $79 right now.\nL162: \nL163:     * BleepingComputer Deals\nL164:     * September 01, 2026\nL165:     * 07:09 AM\nL166:     * cite43†0 L167: \nL168:   * #### cite44†Anthropic is cutting Claude Code's current weekly limits by 17% L169: Anthropic is permanently increasing Claude Code's standard weekly usage limits by 25% for Pro, Max, Team, and seat-based Enterprise plans, but it's not as good as it sounds.\nL170: \nL171:     * cite11†Mayank Parmar L172:     * August 29, 2026\nL173:     * 07:11 PM\nL174:     * cite45†3 L175: \nL176:   * 1\nL177:   * cite46†2 L178:   * cite47†3 L179:   * cite48†4 L180:   * cite49†5 L181:   *   *   Upcoming Webinar\nL182: \nL183: Popular Stories\nL184:   * cite50†Gyazo server flaw exploited to steal 23.6 million user records L185:   * cite51†Fake LastPass Authenticator GitHub repos push new Rapuncel infostealer L186:   * cite52†ShinyHunters hacks Clop leak site, threatens to extort ransomware gang L187: ##### Follow us:\nL188: \nL189: ##### Main Sections\nL190: \nL191:   * cite53†News L192:   * cite54†Webinars L193:   * cite55†VPN Buyer Guides L194:   * cite56†SysAdmin Software Guides L195:   * cite57†Downloads L196:   * cite58†Virus Removal Guides L197:   * cite59†Tutorials L198:   * cite60†Startup Database L199:   * cite61†Uninstall Database L200:   * cite62†Glossary L201: \nL202: ##### Community\nL203: \nL204:   * cite63†Forums L205:   * cite64†Forum Rules L206:   * cite65†Chat L207: \nL208: ##### Useful Resources\nL209: \nL210:   * cite66†Welcome Guide L211:   * cite67†Sitemap --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRelease notes  |  Gemini API  |  Google AI for Developers (https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog)\nciteturn992view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/changelog\",\"lineno\":185}); Total lines: 967\nL156: Both model endpoints accept text, image, video, and audio inputs and support function calling with blocking behavior for physical robot actions. To get started, see the cite24†Gemini Robotics ER overview . For real-time streaming use cases, see cite25†Robotics with streaming .\nL157: \nL158:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` model will be cite26†shut down on August 31, 2026.\nL159: ## July 21, 2026\nL160: \nL161:   * Gemini 3.6 Flash and Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite generally available (GA): Released stable, production-ready versions of our latest 3.x Flash models:\nL162:     * Gemini 3.6 Flash (`gemini-3.6-flash`): Features improved token efficiency and code/agentic planning capabilities at a lower price point than 3.5 Flash, resolving developer feedback around output verbosity.\nL163:     * Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite (`gemini-3.5-flash-lite`): Offers a low-latency, highly cost-effective subagent option designed for high-volume automation.\nL164: \nL165: To learn more, see the cite16†Latest Gemini model guide.\nL166:   * Deprecated parameters: The sampling parameters `temperature`, `top_p` and `top_k` are now deprecated. See the cite27†Latest Gemini Model for details.\nL167: ## July 6, 2026\nL168: \nL169:   * cite28†Developer logs support for the Interactions API: logs for supported Interactions API calls are now viewable in the cite29†AI Studio dashboard†aistudio.google.com .\nL170: ## June 30, 2026\nL171: \nL172:   * Gemini Omni Flash in public preview: Released `gemini-omni-flash-preview`, a high-performance multimodal model designed for high-speed video generation and conversational video editing. Using the cite30†Interactions API , you can generate 3–10 second videos at 720p from text descriptions or animate still images, and then conversationally edit and refine the outputs. To get started, see the cite19†Gemini Omni Flash guide and the cite18†Gemini Omni Flash model card.\nL173:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-image` (Nano Banana 2 Lite) to general availability (GA), our built-in multimodal model optimized for ultra-low latency and cost-effective image generation and editing. See the cite31†Gemini 3.1 Flash Lite Image model card and the cite32†Image generation guide.\nL174: ## June 24, 2026\nL175: \nL176:   * Computer Use: Launched public preview support for the cite33†Computer Use tool in Gemini 3.5 Flash. This release includes simplified actions with intents, built-in support for browser, mobile, and desktop environments, configurable safety policies, and advanced prompt injection detection.\nL177: ## June 17, 2026\nL178: \nL179:   * Streaming support for speech generation: Streaming via `streamGenerateContent` (and `stream: true` in the Interactions API) is now supported for the `gemini-3.1-flash-tts-preview` model. To learn more, see the cite34†Text-to-Speech guide.\nL180: ## June 15, 2026\nL181: \nL182:   * Deprecation announcement: The following image generation models are being deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on August 17, 2026:\nL183: \nL184:     * Imagen 4 and Gemini 3 Image models:\nL185:       * `imagen-4.0-generate-001`\nL186:       * `imagen-4.0-ultra-generate-001`\nL187:       * `imagen-4.0-fast-generate-001`\nL188: \nL189: To migrate your code to newer stable or preview endpoints, refer to the cite35†Gemini deprecations page.\nL190:   * Deprecation announcement: The following video generation models are being deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on June 30, 2026:\nL191: \nL192:     * Veo models:\nL193:       * `veo-2.0-generate-001`\nL194:       * `veo-3.0-generate-001`\nL195:       * `veo-3.0-fast-generate-001`\nL196: Update your integration to either use the Veo 3.1 preview model IDs (`veo-3.1-generate-preview`, `veo-3.1-fast-generate-preview`) or the 3.1 GA models available through the cite36†Gemini Enterprise Agent Platform†docs.cloud.google.com to avoid service interruptions.\nL197: \nL198:   * Deprecation announcement: The experimental GMP Contextual View tool (a fixed interface for Grounding with Google Maps outputs) will cite26†shut down on June 15, 2026:\nL199: ## June 1, 2026\nL200: \nL201:   * The following Gemini 2.0 models are now cite26†shut down :\nL202: \nL203:     * `gemini-2.0-flash`\nL204:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-001`\nL205:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite`\nL206:     * `gemini-2.0-flash-lite-001`\nL207: \nL208: Use cite37†`gemini-3.5-flash` or cite38†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL209: ## May 28, 2026\nL210: \nL211:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-image` (Nano Banana 2) and `gemini-3-pro-image` (Nano Banana Pro), the generally available (GA) versions of our native visual models, cite39†Gemini 3.1 Flash Image and cite40†Gemini 3 Pro Image .\nL212:   * Video-to-image generation support: You can now pass a video file (via direct upload or as a public YouTube URL) as multimodal context alongside a text prompt to generate high-quality thumbnails, cinematic movie posters, or summary infographics. This feature is supported exclusively on the `gemini-3.1-flash-image` model. To learn more, see the cite41†Video-to-image generation guide.\nL213:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-image-preview` and `gemini-3-pro-image-preview` models are deprecated and will be cite26†shut down on June 25, 2026.\nL214: ## May 25, 2026\nL215: \nL216:   * The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model has been cite26†shut down . Use cite38†`gemini-3.1-flash-lite` instead.\nL217: ## May 19, 2026\nL218: \nL219:   * Released `gemini-3.5-flash`, the generally available (GA) version of cite37†Gemini 3.5 Flash , our most intelligent model for sustained frontier performance on agentic and coding tasks. This is now the model behind `gemini-flash-latest`.\nL220:   * Launched the Managed Agents in the Gemini API in public preview. This enables developers to build and deploy autonomous, stateful agents that run in secure, isolated Google-hosted Linux sandbox environments. To learn more, see the cite42†Agents overview page and the cite43†Quickstart .\nL221:   * Released the general-purpose Antigravity Agent managed agent, cite44†`antigravity-preview-05-2026` , in public preview. The Antigravity agent can autonomously plan, reason, write and execute code, manage files, and browse the web inside its sandbox container. See the cite7†Antigravity Agent guide for code samples and specifications.\nL222: ## May 7, 2026\nL223: \nL224:   * Released `gemini-3.1-flash-lite`, the generally available (GA) version of cite38†Gemini 3.1 Flash-Lite , optimized for speed, scale, and cost efficiency.\nL225: \nL226:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-3.1-flash-lite-preview` model is deprecating on 5/11/26 and will be cite26†shut down on May 25, 2026.\nL227: ## May 6, 2026\nL228: \nL229:   * Upcoming breaking change: The cite30†Interactions API request and response schema (`outputs` → `steps`) and output format configuration (`response_format`) are changing. The new schema becomes the default on May 26 and the legacy schema will be removed on June 8. See the cite45†migration guide for details.\nL230: ## May 5, 2026\nL231: \nL232:   * Updated File Search to support multimodal search. You can now natively embed and search through images using the `gemini-embedding-2` model. Grounding metadata now includes `media_id` for visual citations and `page_numbers` that indicate where information is found. To learn more, see the cite46†File Search guide.\nL233: \nL234: ## May 4, 2026\nL235: \nL236:   * Launched event-driven cite47†Webhooks support in the Gemini API to replace polling workflows for the Batch API and long-running operations.\nL237: ## April 30, 2026\nL238: \nL239:   * The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model has been cite26†shut down . Use cite48†`gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview` instead.\nL240: \nL241: ## April 22, 2026\nL242: \nL243:   * Released `gemini-embedding-2` as generally available (GA). To learn more, see the cite49†Embeddings page.\nL244: ## April 21, 2026\nL245: \nL246:   * Released new versions of the cite50†Deep Research agent with collaborative planning, visualization support, MCP server integration, and File Search:\nL247: \nL248:     * cite51†`deep-research-preview-04-2026` : Designed for speed and efficiency, ideal to be streamed back to a client UI.\nL249:     * cite52†`deep-research-max-preview-04-2026` : Maximum comprehensiveness for automated context gathering and synthesis.\nL250: ## April 15, 2026\nL251: \nL252:   * Launched cite53†Gemini 3.1 Flash TTS Preview , our cost-efficient, expressive, and steerable text to speech model. Read the cite54†Text-to-Speech docs to learn more.\nL253: ## April 14, 2026\nL254: \nL255:   * Released `gemini-robotics-er-1.6-preview`, our updated robotics model. It now has new capabilities like instrument reading, improved spatial and physical reasoning capabilities. To learn more, see cite24†Gemini Robotics ER page and the cite55†blog†deepmind.google .\nL256: \nL257:   * Deprecation announcement: The `gemini-robotics-er-1.5-preview` model will be cite26†shut down on April 30, 2026 at 9AM PST.\nL258: ## April 2, 2026\nL259: \nL260:   * Released `gemma-4-26b-a4b-it` and `gemma-4-31b-it`, available on cite56†AI Studio†aistudio.google.com and through the Gemini API, as part of the cite57†Gemma 4 launch.\nL261: \nL262: ## April 1, 2026\nL263: \nL264:   * Introduced the new cite58†Flex and cite59†Priority inference tiers, offering more options for optimizing cost or latency.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nPress Releases | Federal Trade Commission (https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases)\nciteturn992view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ftc.gov/news-events/news/press-releases\",\"lineno\":70}); Total lines: 189\nL0: cite0†iframe†www.googletagmanager.com cite1†Skip to main content L1: \nL2: Displaying 1 - 20 of 11090\nL3: \nL4: Show: [Select]\nL5: \nL6: cite2†Press Release L7: ### cite3†FleetCor Agrees to Pay $100 Million to Resolve Administrative Action After Federal Court Finds that It Violated the FTC Act by Charging Unauthorized Fees L8: \nL9: Date\nL10: \nL11: September 17, 2026\nL12: \nL13: FleetCor and its CEO will pay $100 million to settle a Federal Trade Commission administrative action alleging that the company charged its customers, who overwhelmingly are small businesses...\nL14: \nL15: cite2†Press Release L16: ### cite4†FTC Takes Historic Action Against Multilevel Marketing Operator Amway for Unfair and Deceptive Business Practices L17: \nL18: Date\nL19: \nL20: September 17, 2026\nL21: \nL22: Amway Corp., one of the largest multilevel marketing companies in the U.S., and two of its affiliates—World Wide Group, L.L.C. (WWG) and Leadership Team Development Inc. (LTD)—will pay $225 million to...\nL23: \nL24: cite2†Press Release L25: ### cite5†FTC Announces Additional Payments to Consumers Stemming from FTC’s Amazon Prime Settlement L26: \nL27: Date\nL28: \nL29: September 17, 2026\nL30: \nL31: The Federal Trade Commission announced today that Amazon will accelerate and expand p